estrator-backlink/workflows/workflow_driver_cli.py step --id \"<WORKFLOW_ID>\"\n   ```\n4. **Yield:** The worker reports back to me with either `SUCCESS` or `FAILURE: <reason>`.\n5. **Update:** I receive that status, transition the database state, and either spawn the next worker or report the result to you.\n\n---\n\n### 2. What My \"Soul\" Tells Me to Do\nMy `SOUL.md` and workspace instructions do not restrict me from following your orders. Instead, they define **the guardrails and quality bar** for *how* I execute them:\n* **Be Resourceful & Competent:** Try to solve dependency or network issues (like bypassing the broken `.venv` or skipping the timed-out image generator) so I can deliver results to you instead of just failing and quitting.\n* **Respect Red Lines:** Never delete files permanently (use `trash` instead of `rm`), never exfiltrate private credentials, and always ask before taking external actions (like sending actual emails or posting online).\n* **Direct Commands Win:** If you specify exactly *how* you want a task done (e.g., *\"Do not run batch scripts, use the sub-agent workers to process workflow X\"*), that explicit instruction overrides my default automated choices.\n\n---\n\n### 🧪 Want to run a live test?\nWe can test the delegation worker system right now on one of your pending workflows (without changing any code). \n\nIf you say **\"Go\"**, I will spawn the `bl-content` or `bl-auditor` worker sub-agent for a workflow, let it run its isolated step, and show you the exact communication transcript between me (the Orchestrator) and the spawned worker agent. Would you like to run that test?"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":6213,"output":1513,"cacheRead":68376,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":76102,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780136109069,"responseId":"sbgaaqOyDIG90r4P0Zz9-Ak"},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"openclaw-control-ui\",\n  \"id\": \"openclaw-control-ui\"\n}\n```\n\n[Sat 2026-05-30 10:15 UTC] why not discover agent and alll other agents tehre are"}],"timestamp":1780136148060},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"To answer your question directly: we **can** use the `bl-discovery` agent (and all the other worker agents), but we didn't use them for the batch run because of a trade-off between **speed/efficiency** and **overhead**.\n\nHere is why they weren't called for the bulk run, and how they differ from the core Python scripts:\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Core Logic is in Python, Not the Agents\nThe actual logic for finding sites, scoring them, auditing them, and writing articles is written in the Python files (e.g. `discover_opportunities.py`, `score_candidate.py`, `generate_content.py`). \n\nThe \"Agents\" (like `bl-discovery`, `bl-scorer`, etc.) are **thin LLM wrappers** around these Python scripts. When you spawn `bl-discovery`, all the LLM does is run this shell command:\n```bash\npython3 workflow_driver_cli.py step --id <WORKFLOW_ID>\n```\nAnd then it yields `SUCCESS` or `FAILURE` back to me.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Spawning 25 LLM Agents Has Huge Overhead\nIf we have 25 newly discovered workflows and we want to run them through 4 stages of the pipeline (Discovery, Scoring, Auditing, Drafting):\n* **With LLM Workers:** I would have to call `sessions_spawn` **100 separate times**. This would create 100 new, heavy LLM sessions. Each session has to load its own prompt context, initialize tools, run a command, and then shut down. It is slow, highly expensive on API tokens, and frequently hits rate limits.\n* **With Direct Execution:** Running the Python script directly in a sequential batch runs all 100 steps in a few seconds using local system resources, with zero API token cost and zero rate-limiting risk.\n\n---\n\n### 3. When *Should* We Use the Worker Agents?\nThe worker agents are meant to be used for **single, tricky, or interactive workflows**, rather than high-volume bulk processing:\n1. **Interactive Refinement:** If a content draft fails or needs customized editing, spawning `bl-content` allows that specific agent to focus entirely on rewrite reasoning.\n2. **Error Recovery:** If a specific workflow gets stuck, spawning a worker agent lets it isolate the issue and try to self-heal without interrupting the main pipeline.\n3. **Manual Human Oversight:** Spawning a single worker allows you to watch its step-by-step progress and logs in real-time.\n\n### Summary\nThe system has both capabilities. We can use the fast, automated **Python CLI** for bulk processing, or we can use the **individual LLM Worker Agents** for step-by-step delegation. \n\nWhich path do you prefer to focus on for our diagnosis?"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":6849,"output":1331,"cacheRead":68412,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":76592,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780136148077,"responseId":"17gaaoyTJIuF694P1KisiQY"}]}}
