pipeline (Discovery, Scoring, Auditing, Drafting):\n* **With LLM Workers:** I would have to call `sessions_spawn` **100 separate times**. This would create 100 new, heavy LLM sessions. Each session has to load its own prompt context, initialize tools, run a command, and then shut down. It is slow, highly expensive on API tokens, and frequently hits rate limits.\n* **With Direct Execution:** Running the Python script directly in a sequential batch runs all 100 steps in a few seconds using local system resources, with zero API token cost and zero rate-limiting risk.\n\n---\n\n### 3. When *Should* We Use the Worker Agents?\nThe worker agents are meant to be used for **single, tricky, or interactive workflows**, rather than high-volume bulk processing:\n1. **Interactive Refinement:** If a content draft fails or needs customized editing, spawning `bl-content` allows that specific agent to focus entirely on rewrite reasoning.\n2. **Error Recovery:** If a specific workflow gets stuck, spawning a worker agent lets it isolate the issue and try to self-heal without interrupting the main pipeline.\n3. **Manual Human Oversight:** Spawning a single worker allows you to watch its step-by-step progress and logs in real-time.\n\n### Summary\nThe system has both capabilities. We can use the fast, automated **Python CLI** for bulk processing, or we can use the **individual LLM Worker Agents** for step-by-step delegation. \n\nWhich path do you prefer to focus on for our diagnosis?"],"finalPromptText":"Sender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"openclaw-control-ui\",\n  \"id\": \"openclaw-control-ui\"\n}\n```\n\n[Sat 2026-05-30 10:15 UTC] why not discover agent and alll other agents tehre are","itemLifecycle":{"startedCount":0,"completedCount":0,"activeCount":0},"toolMetas":[],"didSendViaMessagingTool":false,"successfulCronAdds":0,"messagingToolSentTexts":[],"messagingToolSentMediaUrls":[],"messagingToolSentTargets":[]}}
