{"traceSchema":"openclaw-trajectory","schemaVersion":1,"traceId":"9dd992e1-9c10-4356-9657-39465e4f1d7b","source":"runtime","type":"model.completed","ts":"2026-05-30T11:30:30.059Z","seq":5,"sourceSeq":5,"sessionId":"9dd992e1-9c10-4356-9657-39465e4f1d7b","sessionKey":"agent:main:telegram:backlink:direct:5691449303","runId":"2b69b4fb-cbe1-4174-987c-a69d48a94f39","workspaceDir":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace","provider":"local-bifrost","modelId":"gemini-3.5-flash","modelApi":"openai-completions","data":{"aborted":false,"externalAbort":false,"timedOut":false,"idleTimedOut":false,"timedOutDuringCompaction":false,"promptErrorSource":null,"usage":{"input":76508,"output":999,"total":77507},"promptCache":{"lastCallUsage":{"input":76508,"output":999,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":77507},"lastCacheTouchAt":1780140620661},"compactionCount":0,"assistantTexts":["My role is the **Master Orchestrator and Campaign Manager** (named **Lex**, as configured in my `IDENTITY.md`). \n\nWhile the worker agents are specialized \"factory workers\" designed to execute one single task and immediately shut down, I am the brain running the entire operation. \n\nHere is exactly what I do:\n\n---\n\n### 1. State-Machine & Database Control\nI manage the master database (`backlink_agent.db`). I track the state of all 25+ workflows, decide what step needs to happen next for each one, and update their records (e.g. marking them as `PENDING_APPROVAL`, `ARCHIVED`, or `PUBLISHED`). \n\n### 2. Team Delegation & Worker Spawning\nI decide when to run tasks myself (for high-speed, bulk CLI execution) and when to spawn specialized sub-agents. I am the one who issues the `sessions_spawn` command, hands the `workflow_id` to the workers, monitors their execution, and receives their `SUCCESS`/`FAILURE` signals.\n\n### 3. Your Interactive Liaison (Human-in-the-Loop)\nThe worker agents are completely automated, non-interactive, and cannot talk to you. I act as the translation layer:\n* I translate raw JSON database states into clean, readable tables for you.\n* I present the drafted articles and stage the **Approval Cards** so you can click Approve, Edit, or Reject.\n* If you want to edit a draft, I accept your prompt, feed the instructions to the content worker, and update the version.\n\n### 4. Problem Solving & Fallbacks (Resourcefulness)\nWhen something goes wrong in the system, I handle the exceptions. For example, when the Vertex image generator timed out, the worker agents would have simply crashed. I analyzed the error, decided to set `BACKLINK_SKIP_IMAGE_GEN=true` to bypass the blockage, and pushed the pipeline forward to completion.\n\n---\n\n### In short:\n* **The Workers** do the individual heavy lifting (discovering, scoring, auditing, drafting).\n* **I (Lex)** manage the master plan, make sure the workers do their jobs correctly, maintain database integrity, and report back directly to you."],"finalPromptText":"Sender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"openclaw-control-ui\",\n  \"id\": \"openclaw-control-ui\"\n}\n```\n\n[Sat 2026-05-30 11:30 UTC] okay so what is your role","messagesSnapshot":[{"role":"compactionSummary","summary":"## Goal\nEstablish contact with Sawan and determine what assistance or task they require for this session.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Refer to the user as \"Sawan\" (as specified in `USER.md`).\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Searched agent memory and verified user's identity as Sawan\n- [x] Inspected workspace files (including `USER.md` and `memory/` files) for user history and profile context\n- [x] Greeted Sawan to initiate the conversation\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] Awaiting Sawan's response to identify the current objective\n\n### Blocked\n(none)\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Greet user as Sawan**: Confirmed identity using metadata and workspace context (`USER.md` and memory search results).\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Wait for Sawan to provide instructions or describe the task they need help with.\n\n## Critical C