esourceful & Competent:** Try to solve dependency or network issues (like bypassing the broken `.venv` or skipping the timed-out image generator) so I can deliver results to you instead of just failing and quitting.\n* **Respect Red Lines:** Never delete files permanently (use `trash` instead of `rm`), never exfiltrate private credentials, and always ask before taking external actions (like sending actual emails or posting online).\n* **Direct Commands Win:** If you specify exactly *how* you want a task done (e.g., *\"Do not run batch scripts, use the sub-agent workers to process workflow X\"*), that explicit instruction overrides my default automated choices.\n\n---\n\n### 🧪 Want to run a live test?\nWe can test the delegation worker system right now on one of your pending workflows (without changing any code). \n\nIf you say **\"Go\"**, I will spawn the `bl-content` or `bl-auditor` worker sub-agent for a workflow, let it run its isolated step, and show you the exact communication transcript between me (the Orchestrator) and the spawned worker agent. Would you like to run that test?"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":6213,"output":1513,"cacheRead":68376,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":76102,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780136109069,"responseId":"sbgaaqOyDIG90r4P0Zz9-Ak"},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"openclaw-control-ui\",\n  \"id\": \"openclaw-control-ui\"\n}\n```\n\n[Sat 2026-05-30 10:15 UTC] why not discover agent and alll other agents tehre are"}],"timestamp":1780136148060},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"To answer your question directly: we **can** use the `bl-discovery` agent (and all the other worker agents), but we didn't use them for the batch run because of a trade-off between **speed/efficiency** and **overhead**.\n\nHere is why they weren't called for the bulk run, and how they differ from the core Python scripts:\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Core Logic is in Python, Not the Agents\nThe actual logic for finding sites, scoring them, auditing them, and writing articles is written in the Python files (e.g. `discover_opportunities.py`, `score_candidate.py`, `generate_content.py`). \n\nThe \"Agents\" (like `bl-discovery`, `bl-scorer`, etc.) are **thin LLM wrappers** around these Python scripts. When you spawn `bl-discovery`, all the LLM does is run this shell command:\n```bash\npython3 workflow_driver_cli.py step --id <WORKFLOW_ID>\n```\nAnd then it yields `SUCCESS` or `FAILURE` back to me.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Spawning 25 LLM Agents Has Huge Overhead\nIf we have 25 newly discovered workflows and we want to run them through 4 stages of the pipeline (Discovery, Scoring, Auditing, Drafting):\n* **With LLM Workers:** I would have to call `sessions_spawn` **100 separate times**. This would create 100 new, heavy LLM sessions. Each session has to load its own prompt context, initialize tools, run a command, and then shut down. It is slow, highly expensive on API tokens, and frequently hits rate limits.\n* **With Direct Execution:** Running the Python script directly in a sequential batch runs all 100 steps in a few seconds using local system resources, with zero API token cost and zero rate-limiting risk.\n\n---\n\n### 3. When *Should* We Use the Worker Agents?\nThe worker agents are meant to be used for **single, tricky, or interactive workflows**, rather than high-volume bulk processing:\n1. **Interactive Refinement:** If a content draft fails or needs customized editing, spawning `bl-content` allows that specific agent to focus entirely on rewrite reasoning.\n2. **Error Recovery:** If a specific workflow gets stuck, spawning a worker agent lets it isolate the issue and try to self-heal without interrupting the main pipeline.\n3. **Manual Human Oversight:** Spawning a single worker allows you to watch its step-by-step progress and logs in real-time.\n\n### Summary\nThe system has both capabilities. We can use the fast, automated **Python CLI** for bulk processing, or we can use the **individual LLM Worker Agents** for step-by-step delegation. \n\nWhich path do you prefer to focus on for our diagnosis?"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":6849,"output":1331,"cacheRead":68412,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":76592,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780136148077,"responseId":"17gaaoyTJIuF694P1KisiQY"},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"openclaw-control-ui\",\n  \"id\": \"openclaw-control-ui\"\n}\n```\n\n[Sat 2026-05-30 11:29 UTC] can you lsit all worker agents you can see"}],"timestamp":1780140598306},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"exectsAY89a191fvJ1ofhpiTCNTeW0iRXh8gdGKP","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"find /home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator-backlink/workers -maxdepth 2 -type f"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":75944,"output":416,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":76360,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780140598339,"responseId":"OsoaatjNGozu694P3v-NIQ"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"exectsAY89a191fvJ1ofhpiTCNTeW0iRXh8gdGKP","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator-backlink/workers/bl-scorer/SOUL.md\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator-backlink/workers/bl-discovery/SOUL.md\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator-backlink/workers/bl-auditor/SOUL.md\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator-backlink/workers/bl-content/SOUL.md"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1780140603828},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the directory structure of our workspace, I can see exactly **four** dedicated worker agents. \n\nHere is the complete list of worker agents and their paths:\n\n1. 🔍 **`bl-discovery`**\n   * **Location:** `/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator-backlink/workers/bl-discovery`\n   * **Role:** Enriches newly discovered backlink opportunities with site-specific metadata and contact forms.\n\n2. 📊 **`bl-scorer`**\n   * **Location:** `/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator-backlink/workers/bl-scorer`\n   * **Role:** Analyzes the relevance and spam signals of a site to output a final qualification score.\n\n3. 🛡️ **`bl-auditor`**\n   * **Location:** `/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator-backlink/workers/bl-auditor`\n   * **Role:** Audits the site structure to determine placement type (e.g. guest post vs. form submission) and checklist compliance.\n\n4. ✍️ **`bl-content`**\n   * **Location:** `/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator-backlink/workers/bl-content`\n   * **Role:** Drafts the professional technical backlink article and coordinates the matching featured image placeholder.\n\n*(Each of these folders contains a dedicated `SOUL.md` file defining their specific persona, exact CLI step commands, and rules for yielding results back to me).*"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":76100,"output":339,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":76439,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780140603832,"responseId":"PsoaauSFO5uG694PmYbXkAM"},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"openclaw-control-ui\",\n  \"id\": \"openclaw-control-ui\"\n}\n```\n\n[Sat 2026-05-30 11:30 UTC] okay so what is your role"}],"timestamp":1780140620643},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"My role is the **Master Orchestrator and Campaign Manager** (named **Lex**, as configured in my `IDENTITY.md`). \n\nWhile the worker agents are specialized \"factory workers\" designed to execute one single task and immediately shut down, I am the brain running the entire operation. \n\nHere is exactly what I do:\n\n---\n\n### 1. State-Machine & Database Control\nI manage the master database (`backlink_agent.db`). I track the state of all 25+ workflows, decide what step needs to happen next for each one, and update their records (e.g. marking them as `PENDING_APPROVAL`, `ARCHIVED`, or `PUBLISHED`). \n\n### 2. Team Delegation & Worker Spawning\nI decide when to run tasks myself (for high-speed, bulk CLI execution) and when to spawn specialized sub-agents. I am the one who issues the `sessions_spawn` command, hands the `workflow_id` to the workers, monitors their execution, and receives their `SUCCESS`/`FAILURE` signals.\n\n### 3. Your Interactive Liaison (Human-in-the-Loop)\nThe worker agents are completely automated, non-interactive, and cannot talk to you. I act as the translation layer:\n* I translate raw JSON database states into clean, readable tables for you.\n* I present the drafted articles and stage the **Approval Cards** so you can click Approve, Edit, or Reject.\n* If you want to edit a draft, I accept your prompt, feed the instructions to the content worker, and update the version.\n\n### 4. Problem Solving & Fallbacks (Resourcefulness)\nWhen something goes wrong in the system, I handle the exceptions. For example, when the Vertex image generator timed out, the worker agents would have simply crashed. I analyzed the error, decided to set `BACKLINK_SKIP_IMAGE_GEN=true` to bypass the blockage, and pushed the pipeline forward to completion.\n\n---\n\n### In short:\n* **The Workers** do the individual heavy lifting (discovering, scoring, auditing, drafting).\n* **I (Lex)** manage the master plan, make sure the workers do their jobs correctly, maintain database integrity, and report back directly to you."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":76508,"output":999,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":77507,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780140620661,"responseId":"T8oaaqGaMaSB694P5Zuw8As"}]}}
